The ``SignalHoundUSBSA124B`` driver now logs through its instrument logger, so that it does not log
while the garbage collector closes it. Its log records are therefore emitted by the
``qcodes.instrument.instrument_base`` logger with the name of the instrument, rather than by the
logger of the driver module. ``SignalHoundUSBSA124B.check_for_error`` takes an optional ``logger``,
which the driver passes when it calls the method itself, so subclasses that override
``check_for_error`` must accept it too.
